<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05S1">Variant <span data-tag="05S1">7.4.4.14</span>.</a> Let $\lambda $ be an uncountable cardinal of exponential cofinality $\kappa = \mathrm{ecf}(\lambda )$ and suppose we are given a diagram $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda }$, where $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a $\kappa $-small simplicial set. It follows from the proof of Proposition <a data-tag="05RX" href="/tag/05RX">7.4.4.1</a> (together with Remark <a data-tag="02TH" href="/tag/02TH">7.4.4.13</a>) that the diagram $\mathscr {F}$ admits a limit $\varprojlim (\mathscr {F} )$, which can be identified with $\operatorname{Fun}^{\operatorname{CCart}}_{ /\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}, \operatorname{\mathcal{E}})$ for any cocartesian fibration $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ with covariant transport representation $\mathscr {F}$ (for example. we can take $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}= \int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F}$). In particular, the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda }$ admits $\kappa $-small limits, which are preserved by the inclusion functors $\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \lambda } \hookrightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}_{&lt; \mu }$ for every $\mu \geq \lambda $. </p>
